+## 10. The camera at her eye's grain (2026-09-16)
+
+The page sends the camera's whole frame resampled to her 160 × 120 field (letterboxed in black if the camera is wider than 4:3), with the 135 ambient sites first: 58,005 values, about 77 KB as base64 in one occurrence (cap 128 KiB). The server keeps a frame at least her eye's size at her grain (`EXTERNAL_RGB_FULL_VALUE_COUNT`) and resamples a smaller crop (an older page, the caretaker's cards) onto the 80 × 60 field the beat tiles 2 × 2. Her beat takes the full frame as her focal field as sent, after eyelid transmission. The frame is the camera's fixed carriage (the camera does not turn), so her gaze within the field is her gaze in the frame: the crop's share of the frame is its per-site pitch times its site count over the declared 60° × 45° field, and a share of one or more engages the whole-frame law. The page keeps her world field in its own slot every beat, camera on or off. Test: `test_the_cameras_whole_frame_at_her_eyes_grain_is_her_focal_field_as_sent`.
